A||N||12||Vlad||Swapping seats??||||1||
Z||000000||Vlad||10-23-2000||10:52 PM||||Hello<P>Can I swap seat from passanger side with driver side seat? They seem to be the same...<BR>Arn't they?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||10-23-2000||11:16 PM||||I wondered that myself, but I think I remember being told once that you cant swap them. My pass. seat is in great condition, but the drivers side is torn.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000002||Vlad||10-23-2000||11:34 PM||||Same here.<P>I don't see why they cannot be swaped. They seem to be absolutely same.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_Freak||10-23-2000||11:46 PM||||Is there any problem with the reclining release on the side of the seat?||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||10-23-2000||11:48 PM||||You can swap the "skins".....they are identical.  The seats themselves are different though.  The recline mechanism is on the wrong side to swap easily.  <P>That said, it is still possible to swap the entire seat from passenger to driver and vice versa.  You will need to remove the recline handle assembly and remove the seat back from the bottom.  Remove the nut plate thing that the bolts screw into (you will need to swap them as the outer side of the seat bottom has 2 bolts and the inside only one).  It is quite a chore to do and is just easier to swap the skins, but it is possible.<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Vlad||10-24-2000||12:16 AM||||Strange....<P>Haynes manual shows that there is a even numbers of holes on the bottom of the seat.<P>Anyway, I will try to do that swap and I will report the result.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||10-24-2000||01:13 AM||||The holes are there, but the nut plate things aren't.  You will need to swap these over to install all of the mechanisms & whatnot.  A pretty easy thing to do, but confusing and difficult to describe.||||reg||10
Z||000007||Vlad||10-24-2000||01:39 AM||||I just checked it.<P>Are you saying that there are ready holes for the reclining release nut plate on the opposite side of the seat. Then it makes job quite easy. No drilling....))  Will release directly bolt on  on the opposite side?<P>Also, to unscrew two bolts from the upper part of the seat I will have to pull up its cover. Am I<BR>right? Oh... One more thing. There is a spring which seems to be very heavy. How difficult is it to remove it once the seat is out of the car?||||reg||1
Z||000008||286SE'S||10-24-2000||04:15 PM||||This has been covered before. they cannot be swapped. On the top seatback, on the inner console side it has has one hole for a big bolt that is just a pivot point. That hole is not present on the outer/recline lever side. Just swap the skins and wash them while they are off. Learning how to pull/replace seat skins is just one of those skills every Fiero owner should learn.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tigger||10-24-2000||04:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 286SE'S:<BR><B>This has been covered before. they cannot be swapped.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Translation, the passenger seat skin can be transferred to the drivers seat, but not from the drivers seat to the passenger side.  Theoretically you could transfer the drivers seat to the passenger side, but you'd have a hole showing, right?<P>90% of the time the driver's seat takes the puke because of obvious reasons, and there are 60% more passenger seats that are in good condition that could be used for the swap.  Here I go again with my "fuzzy" math  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||10-25-2000||02:19 AM||||The seat back skins are interchangable. The seat bottoms can be swapped but you will have 2 holes on the side that faces the console. Unseen but they will be there. You cannot swap seat frames.||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfiero||10-25-2000||03:36 AM||||It seems was in error with my previous statement.  You can't swap seatbacks, just the skins.  However, you can swap the seat bottoms.  The bottoms are the ones with the holes already there.  Oreif is correct, there will be extra holes in the skin, but they will not be noticeable.  The center console  covers one side and the spring mechanism cover covers the other.<P>Sorry for any confusion.||||reg||1
Z||000012||fldevel||10-26-2000||12:54 PM||||i think i remember trying this once before ... the problem i ran into was that the two bolts closest to the door where about 1" closer together then the two bolts closest to the console ... ||||reg||1
